  "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)\u2248f(a,b,c)+\u2207f(a,b,c)\\cdot \u27e8x-a,y-b,z-c\u27e9.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(3,0,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & \u2248f(3,0,4)+\u2207f(3,0,4)\\cdot \u27e8x-3,y-0,z-4\u27e9 \\\\  & =25+\u27e8{f}_{x}(3,0,4),{f}_{y}(3,0,4),{f}_{z}(3,0,4)\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-3,y,z-4\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(3,0,4)$, ${f}_{y}(3,0,4)$ and ${f}_{z}(3,0,4),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(3)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=3 \\\\ {f}_{y}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(0)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=0 \\\\ {f}_{z}(3,0,4) & =\\frac{5(4)}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}}}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)\u224825+\u27e83,0,4\u27e9\\cdot \u27e8x-3,y,z-4\u27e9.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(3.01,0.1,3.99)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=3.01,y=0.1$ and $z=3.99,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.01,0.1,3.99) & \u224825+\u27e83,0,4\u27e9\\cdot \u27e83.01-3,0.1,3.99-4\u27e9 \\\\  & =25+\u27e83,0,4\u27e9\\cdot \u27e80.01,0.1,-0.01\u27e9 \\\\  & =25+0.03-0.04 \\\\  & =24.99\\end{aligned}\n$$",
